\chapter{Documents and the Session Model}\label{ch:model}

With the numeric core in place, we turn to the app. This chapter describes the data the user
interface is built on: the scenes that make up the app, the document that brings an image in,
the small value types that describe images, zones and panes, and the [[Session]], the one
object per window that holds everything the views show.

\section{The app and its scenes}

A SwiftUI app is a list of \emph{scenes}, each a kind of window. LineScope has four.
\begin{description}[style=nextline]
\item[Image documents] One window per opened image file, supplied by [[DocumentGroup]] in its
  \emph{viewing} form: the app opens documents but never creates or saves them, so there is no
  New or Save command to disable.
\item[Test patterns] One window per generated pattern (Chapter~\ref{ch:patterns}). A
  [[WindowGroup]] keyed by a [[TestPatternSpec]] value opens a new window for each spec; because
  the spec is [[Codable]], macOS can restore these windows after a relaunch.
\item[Pattern generator] A single window for choosing a pattern and its parameters.
\item[Inspector] A single window describing the image in focus, placed at the top right.
\end{description}
The menus of Chapter~\ref{ch:commands} are attached to the document scene, which puts them in the
app's menu bar.

<<LineScope/LineScopeApp.swift>>=
import LineScopeCore
import SwiftUI

@main
struct LineScopeApp: App {
    var body: some Scene {
        <<LineScopeApp: document windows>>

        <<LineScopeApp: test-pattern windows>>

        <<LineScopeApp: pattern generator window>>

        <<LineScopeApp: inspector window>>
    }
}
@

A document window gets the document and a name to show and export under. The file name falls back
to ``Untitled'' for documents without a URL.

<<LineScopeApp: document windows>>=
DocumentGroup(viewing: ImageDocument.self) { file in
    MainView(document: file.document, fileName: file.fileURL?.lastPathComponent ?? "Untitled")
}
.defaultSize(width: 1100, height: 900)
.commands { LineScopeCommands() }
@

The window group passes a binding to an optional spec, which is [[nil]] only in the moment before
SwiftUI has decoded a restored window's value; nothing is shown then.

<<LineScopeApp: test-pattern windows>>=
WindowGroup("Test Pattern", for: TestPatternSpec.self) { $spec in
    if let spec {
        PatternWindow(spec: spec)
    }
}
.defaultSize(width: 1100, height: 900)
@

<<LineScopeApp: pattern generator window>>=
Window("New Test Pattern", id: TestPatternGeneratorView.windowID) {
    TestPatternGeneratorView()
}
.windowResizability(.contentSize)
@

<<LineScopeApp: inspector window>>=
Window("Inspector", id: InspectorView.windowID) {
    InspectorView()
}
.defaultSize(width: 340, height: 760)
.defaultPosition(.topTrailing)
